WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.152
Duplicate detection depends on the identity rule.

00:00:03.152 --> 00:00:08.112
Email alone may be useful but can fail when emails are shared or changed.

00:00:08.112 --> 00:00:13.387
Name plus email can be stronger but may miss rows with incomplete values.

00:00:13.387 --> 00:00:18.662
Phone can provide supporting evidence but is not perfect.

00:00:18.662 --> 00:00:22.332
For sensitive data, possible duplicates often need multiple signals and review.

00:00:22.332 --> 00:00:27.237
Duplicate resolution requires a definition of identity and a survivor rule.

00:00:27.237 --> 00:00:32.722
Exact duplicate rows are easy; duplicate people or customers are harder.

00:00:32.722 --> 00:00:40.437
If you choose one survivor, document the priority—latest update, verified source, highest completeness,

00:00:40.437 --> 00:00:44.400
or another defensible rule—and preserve links to the merged records.
